                             Virtual Private Cloud

--> VPC is a virtual network or data center for one client
--> it is logically isolated from other virtual betwork in the AWWS Cloud
--> once we created VPC, DHCP, security group and NACL will be automatically created
DHCP: Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol

--> VPC types:
1. Default VPC
2. Custom VPC

--> up to 5 VPC you can create per region and 200 subnets in 1 VPC
--> once the VPC is created, you can not chnaged its CIDR block
--> if you need differnt CIDR size, then create new VPC
--> different subnet within a VPC can not overlap

--> steps to create VPC:
1. create VPC  
    -----> 1. VPC name
    -----> 2. VPC CIDR --> 10.0.0.0/16 ---> 65536

2. create subnet
--> subnet means sub network
--> subnet is a range of an ip address
--> subnetting --> is the process of dividing large network into smaller one
--> why?? 
    ---> can help to reduce the congesion
    ---> better IP allocation
    ---> better security

-----------> 1. subnet name
-----------> 2. Subnet CIDR --> 10.0.0.0/20

--> types of subnet:
1. Public Subnet
2. Private Subnet

3. Internet Gateway
--> gateway is used to connect two different network
--> An internet gateway is a virtual router that connects a VPC to the internet. 

4. Route table
----> to select subnet association
----> enter routes

--> Jump server/basion  host
----> A Jump Server is an EC2 instance placed in a public subnet 
that you use to connect to resources in a private subnet.
----> You cannot directly SSH from the Internet to the private EC2 because it has no public IP. 


--> NAT gateway:
----> A NAT Gateway is used when resources in a private subnet need to access the Internet,
 while preventing the Internet from initiating connections directly to those private resources.
----> A NAT Gateway itself needs Internet connectivity.
So it is normally created in a public subnet and associated with an Elastic IP.

** VPC Peering:
---> A VPC peering connection is a networking connection between two VPCs that enables you to route traffic between them privately.
