IP addresses:
1. Public IP Address:
--> A public IP allows an EC2 instance to communicate with the Internet.
--> This is very important. If you stop an EC2 instance and start it again,
its public IPv4 address can change.

2. Private IP Address:
--> A private IP is an IP address used for communication inside your VPC/private network.
--> By default, the primary private IPv4 address is persistent for the life of the EC2 instance.

3. Elastic IP:
--> An Elastic IP (EIP) is a static public IPv4 address that you allocate to your AWS account.
--> Elastic IP does not normally change when you stop and start the EC2 instance.


